                Carmelo R. Cartiere,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formal Methods for Quantum Software Engineering
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Software Engineering
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-05324-5_5"} doi:10.1007/978-3-031-05324-5_5
              %blockquote
                %p “The characteristic difficulty in creating pure quantum software is mainly due to the inaccessibility to intermediate states, which makes debugging practically impossible. However, the use of formal methods, which apply rigorous mathematical models to ensure error-free software, can overcome this barrier and enable the production of reliable quantum algorithms and applications right out of the box.”
